rpose |\n126: |------|---------|\n127: | `--apps` | Run interactive app picker after core install |\n128: | `--full` | Core install + all apps (non-interactive) |\n129: | `--dry-run` | Preview without executing |\n130: | `--skip <phase>` | Skip a phase (repeatable): `preinstall`, `scripts`, `postinstall`, `scalepoint`, `apps` |\n131: | `--steps <spec>` | Run only specific phases. Format: `1,3,4` or `1-3` |\n132: | `--no-color` | Disable colored output |\n133: \n134: ### pos Output Logging\n135: \n136: All non-interactive `pos` commands log output to `~/.local/share/linux_post_install/logs/`:\n137: - Per-command files: `YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_pos_<cmd>.log` (full stdout+stderr)\n138: - Main log: `pos.log` (command + timestamp + exit code for every invocation)\n139: - Interactive commands (`system-firewall`, `media-mp4`) only log invocation, not output\n140: \n141: ---\n142: \n143: ## 4. The `pos` CLI System\n144: \n145: ### How It Works\n146: \n147: `bin/pos` is the main dispatcher. It:\n148: 1. Scans its own directory for all executable `pos-*` files\n149: 2. Extracts category-subcommand names from filenames\n150: 3. Uses variable-length argument matching to find the right script\n151: \n152: **Example:** `pos docker compose up jellyfin`\n153: - Tries `pos-docker-compose-up-jellyfin` (not found)\n154: - Tries `pos-docker-compose-up` (not found)\n155: - Finds `pos-docker-compose` (runs with args `up jellyfin`)\n156: \n157: ### Available Commands\n158: \n159: | Category | Command | Script | Description |\n160: |----------|---------|--------|-------------|\n161: | network | ip | `pos-network-ip` | Show interfaces, routes, public IP |\n162: | network | checkport | `pos-network-checkport` | Check TCP port connectivity |\n163: | network | scan | `pos-network-scan` | Parallel ping sweep of CIDR |\n164: | docker | ps | `pos-docker-ps` | Enhanced container overview |\n165: | docker | health | `pos-docker-health` | Quick health dashboard (exits 1 if unhealthy) |\n166: | docker | compose | `pos-docker-compose` | Service manager (ls/up/down/restart/logs/update/config) |\n167: | media | mp3 | `pos-media-mp3` | Download audio as MP3 |\n168: | media | mp4 | `pos-media-mp4` | Download video with format select |\n169: | system | firewall | `pos-system-firewall` | Interactive UFW management |\n170: | ssh | load-keys | `pos-ssh-load-keys` | Load SSH keys into agent |\n171: | vbox | create | `pos-vbox create` | Create disposable VM (asks \"Enter now?\") |\n172: | vbox | enter | `pos-vbox enter` | Start and exec into container |\n173: | vbox | ls | `pos-vbox ls` | List vbox-managed containers only (label-filtered) |\n174: | vbox | start/stop/rm | `pos-vbox start/stop/rm` | Lifecycle management |\n175: \n176: ### Legacy Wrappers\n177: \n178: These forward to `pos` transparently: `wr-ip`, `wr-checkport`, `wr-scan-ping`, `wr-docker`, `wr-compose`, `wr-ufw`, `mp3`, `mp4`, `vbox`, `ssh-load-all`.\n179: \n180: ### pos vbox Details\n181: \n182: `pos-vbox` manages disposable Docker containers as lightweight VMs:\n183: \n184: - **Container labeling:** All created containers get `linux_post_install.vbox=true` label\n185: - **`ls` filtering:** `docker ps --filter label=linux_post_install.vbox=true` — only shows vbox-managed containers\n186: - **Post-create prompt:** After `create`, asks \"Enter now? [Y/n]\" using `confirm` helper\n187: - **Working dir detection:** `enter` auto-detects bind mount path from container labels\n188: - **Custom dirs:** `--dir <path>` or `--dir .` for current directory\n189: \n190: ---\n191: \n192: ## 5. Shared Library — `lib/common.sh`\n193: \n194: Sourced by most scripts. Provides:\n195: \n196: | Function | Purpose |\n197: |----------|---------|\n198: | `log \"msg\"` | Green `[+]` status message |\n199: | `warn \"msg\"` | Yellow `[!]` warning |\n200: | `err \"msg\"` | Red `ERROR:` + exit 1 |\n201: | `ok \"msg\"` | Green `OK` prefix |\n202: | `section \"title\"` | Cyan-bordered section header |\n203: | `step N T \"msg\"` | Numbered step 