e |\n249: | `pos docker compose logs <svc> [-f]` | View/follow logs |\n250: | `pos docker compose update` | Pull latest templates, refresh compose.yaml (preserves .env) |\n251: | `pos docker compose config set K=V` | Set global config value |\n252: | `pos docker compose config show` | Display current config |\n253: \n254: ### Global Config Keys\n255: \n256: - `TS_AUTHKEY` — Tailscale auth key (required)\n257: - `TZ` — Timezone\n258: - `DNS_SERVER` — Custom DNS\n259: - `SERVICES_BASE` — Deployment root (default: `/srv`)\n260: \n261: ---\n262: \n263: ## 7. Optional Apps (`apps/`)\n264: \n265: ### How They Work\n266: \n267: - `apps/install.sh` auto-discovers all `apps/<category>/*.sh` files (excluding itself)\n268: - Three modes: interactive (default), `--all`, or specific app names as arguments\n269: - Interactive TUI groups apps by category with section headers\n270: - Each app script is standalone, idempotent, sources `lib/common.sh`\n271: \n272: ### Installation Methods\n273: \n274: | Method | Apps |\n275: |--------|------|\n276: | `apt install` | btop, obs, vlc, vnc-viewer, qemu |\n277: | APT repo (GPG + repo) | brave, vscode |\n278: | Official `curl \\| sh` | docker, tailscale, netbird, zerotier, opencode |\n279: | AppImage | affine |\n280: | GitHub release binary | scrcpy |\n281: | Flatpak | localsend |\n282: | .deb package | termius |\n283: \n284: ### Adding a New App\n285: \n286: 1. Create `apps/<name>.sh` following the template in DEV.md\n287: 2. It auto-appears in the interactive picker — no registration needed\n288: \n289: ---\n290: \n291: ## 8. Systemd Services\n292: \n293: | Service | File | Purpose |\n294: |---------|------|---------|\n295: | `ssh-agent.service` | `systemd/ssh-agent.service` | System-wide SSH agent, socket at `/run/ssh-agent/socket` |\n296: | `autostart.service` | `systemd/autostart.service` | Runs `autostart.sh` on boot |\n297: \n298: All `.service` files in `systemd/` are automatically copied to `/etc/systemd/system/` and enabled by `postinstall.sh`.\n299: \n300: ---\n301: \n302: ## 9. Configuration Files\n303: \n304: ### Gitignored Secrets\n305: \n306: - `config/rclone.conf` — rclone remote config (OAuth tokens)\n307: - `config/authorized_keys` — SSH public keys\n308: \n309: ### Runtime Config\n310: \n311: - `~/.config/linux_post_install/compose.env` — Docker Compose global defaults\n312: - `~/.bashrc` — Modified by postinstall (PATH, bash completion)\n313: \n314: ---\n315: \n316: ## 10. Coding Conventions\n317: \n318: ### Script Standards\n319: \n320: - **Shebang:** `#!/usr/bin/env bash`\n321: - **Strict mode:** `set -euo pipefail`\n322: - **Help:** Every script accepts `-h`/`--help` via `case` pattern\n323: - **Idempotency:** Check existence before creating/modifying\n324: - **Exit codes:** 0 = success, 1 = error\n325: \n326: ### Naming Conventions\n327: \n328: - `pos-<category>-<command>` — canonical tool names\n329: - `wr-*` — legacy wrappers\n330: - `apps/<category>/<name>.sh` — optional app installers\n331: - Hyphens for word separation, lowercase always\n332: \n333: ### Error Handling\n334: \n335: - `command -v <tool> &>/dev/null` to check tool availability\n336: - `set -euo pipefail` for fail-fast\n337: - `err()` for fatal errors, `warn()` for non-fatal\n338: - Confirmation prompts for destructive actions\n339: \n340: ### Security\n341: \n342: - Never hardcode secrets in scripts\n343: - Use `chmod 600` for sensitive files\n344: - Validate user input before shell commands\n345: - Use `sudo` only where necessary\n346: \n347: ---\n348: \n349: ## 11. Development Workflow\n350: \n351: ### Adding a New App\n352: \n353: 1. Create `apps/<category>/<name>.sh` following the template in DEV.md\n354: 2. It auto-appears in the interactive picker — no registration needed\n355: \n356: ### Adding a New Tool\n357: \n358: 1. Create `bin/pos-<category>-<command>` following conventions\n359: 2. Add system deps to `PACKAGES` array in `preinstall.sh` (if needed)\n360: 3. Add config logic to `postinstall.sh` (