             # Deploy or start a service\n103: pos docker compose down actual-budget        # Stop a service\n104: pos docker compose logs home-assistant -f    # Tail logs\n105: pos docker compose restart home-assistant    # Restart a service\n106: pos docker compose update                    # Pull latest templates + refresh deployed compose files\n107: pos docker compose config                    # Show current configuration\n108: pos docker compose config set TZ=Asia/Tokyo  # Set a global default\n109: pos docker compose config edit               # Open config in editor\n110: ```\n111: \n112: **Config strategy — three layers:**\n113: \n114: | Layer | File | Purpose |\n115: |-------|------|---------|\n116: | Template defaults | `/usr/local/share/linux_post_install/scale-tail/services/<name>/.env` | Per-service defaults from ScaleTail |\n117: | Global config | `~/.config/linux_post_install/compose.env` | Your defaults — applies to all services |\n118: | Per-service | `/srv/<service>/.env` | Actual config — created on first deploy, **never overwritten** |\n119: \n120: Set global defaults once, then every `up` fills them into the new service's `.env`.\n121: \n122: **Paths:**\n123: \n124: - Templates: `/usr/local/share/linux_post_install/scale-tail/services/`\n125: - Deployments: `/srv/<service>/` (configurable via `SERVICES_BASE`)\n126: - Global config: `~/.config/linux_post_install/compose.env`\n127: \n128: **Config keys:**\n129: \n130: | Key | What it does |\n131: |-----|-------------|\n132: | `TS_AUTHKEY` | Tailscale auth key (required for sidecar networking) |\n133: | `TZ` | Timezone for the service |\n134: | `DNS_SERVER` | Custom DNS server |\n135: | `SERVICES_BASE` | Where services are deployed (default: `/srv`)\n136: \n137: ### VBox (disposable Docker containers)\n138: \n139: ```bash\n140: pos vbox create lab1                         # Create — prompts to enter\n141: pos vbox create lab1 --dir .                 # Bind mount current directory\n142: pos vbox ent